sec 7.4: the retiring seq is taken over the records of the retirement's own second alone; the root's succession at seq 1, a twin of its history, is anchored three seconds after its retirement and leaves the retiring seq at 2, so the succession at 2, bounded only by its own record of that second, is timely and k2 is in the lineage; the seq-1 twin, bounded by nothing in time, RETIRED, and the root's later record DISCARDED.
